    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Statistics, California State University, Bakersfield"
title: "The Shape of Volatility Memory"
year: 2026
abstract: >
  Nonparametric estimation of the ARCH(infinity) memory kernel for 500 financial
  assets finds that 85.2% of 352 identified assets reject geometric (GARCH) decay
  via a correctly-sized parametric bootstrap; the median shape parameter is 0.25,
  indicating sub-exponential memory; true long memory is rare (~3%); no out-of-sample
  forecasting edge over GARCH is found.
journal: "Journal of Applied Econometrics"
type: article
status: submitted
